    {
      "part": "Sea State",
      "number": "5",
      "title": "Sea state scale (state of the sea surface, 0-9)",
      "commentary": [
        "A separate scale from Beaufort: Beaufort describes WIND force, while this scale (WMO/Douglas) describes the actual wave height, which depends not only on the current wind but also on fetch and swell — so the two scales' numbers don't always match.",
        "Height is the significant wave height (average of the highest 1/3 of waves), not the maximum single wave, which can be noticeably higher."
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "head": [
            "Code",
            "Sea state",
            "Wave height"
